# a4kt710: its .moddata keys (amix-dlm C3-1 section 3, C4-2 section 1 and the
# A4000T row of section 8) and the definition line.  One Master for both lines:
# no $cpu, the kit's fragment gives the line's.
# $match mobo:a4000t-710: a registry probe (20 section 6, C2-1 id 3).  A mobo:
# key always matches at load; a4kt710_load is the gate (docs/A4000T-ONBOARD-710.md
# section 10.2) and touches nothing under $DD0000 undeclared.
# $param declared (C4-2 v6 section 8.1): -1 the Kickstart's NCR ROM tag decides,
# 0 never touch the window, 1 a manual override (touch without the tag).
# $param intr: -1 (default, auto) completion on the interrupt once the kernel
# sends a command over 4 KiB through the C4-7 entry (the limits accepted and
# the self-test passed: polled until then, and for good when the limits were
# refused); 1 the interrupt always; 0 polled always.
# $param limits: 1 (default) declare the C4-7 limits after sd_register (one
# segment of up to 64 KiB), 0 declare nothing (the stock page commands).
# $param spin: 0 (default) off; else, with the interrupt on, the queue reads
# the chip for up to that many us after its launch and finishes a command
# that stopped there inline (cap 1000).  spinrd: the spin's ISTAT reads per
# command instead of the beam calibration (0, the default: calibrate).
# $param sync: 0 (default) every target asynchronous; 1 negotiate synchronous
# transfers per target (SDTR, 100 ns offset 8), asynchronous for good after a
# parity error or phase mismatch on a synchronous transfer.
# $rank mobo: sd's class 3 (C4-1 section 4).  No $majors: sd owns them.
# $modtype misc: MOD_HDRV_WRAPPER, no switch-table slot.
$modtype misc
$class root
$match mobo:a4000t-710
$rank mobo
$unload never
$param declared:int:-1:-1:1
$param intr:int:-1:-1:1
$param limits:int:1:0:1
$param spin:int:0:0:1000
$param spinrd:int:0:0:1048576
$param sync:int:0:0:1
$desc A4000T onboard SCSI (NCR 53C710), root-class disk controller
a4kt710	a4kt710
